{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011tTySmzhKvkfos2m3r17g9","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Anchor R&D Surface v12 â€” \"Efforts\" (continuity-first single-session trio) Â· MASTER PLAN\n2\t\n3\t> **Status:** Stage 1 (Master Plan) â€” REVISED after Shark-Tank Round 1 (all 3 Sharks BLOCKed the\n4\t> first \"literally one shared session/worktree/context\" draft; John's lived-workflow evidence\n5\t> reframed the model to **continuity-first with a context-relief handoff**). Approved by John for\n6\t> the model + sequencing 2026-06-21. Frozen design lives here; the wave-by-wave build plan lives in\n7\t> `IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN.md`. Approved mockups: `_mockups/dashboard_D_headline_shelf.html` (dashboard)\n8\t> + `_mockups/grass_2_workbench.html` (grass catcher).\n9\t\n10\t---\n11\t\n12\t## 1. North Star (LOCKED 2026-06-21)\n13\t\n14\t> **Anchor's per-project dashboard lets John run a unit of work as a single continuous \"effort\"\n15\t> that flows Research â†’ Plan â†’ Build in ONE session by default â€” the stage transition is a\n16\t> lightweight relabel, not a managed handoff â€” with a fresh-session handoff only as a\n17\t> context-relief valve, and with every effort's docs, deliverable, and summary durably saved and\n18\t> reopenable, surfaced on the simple Layout-D dashboard.**\n19\t\n20\t### Success criteria (each testable)\n21\t\n22\t- **SC1 â€” Continuity-first in-session stages.** An effort is ONE session by default; you work\n23\t  Râ†’Pâ†’B in the same conversation, each skill loading as the work naturally progresses. \"Advance\"\n24\t  is a **relabel + persist + summarize** of the completed stage â€” it spawns **no new session** and\n25\t  injects **nothing** into your conversation. Advance is auto-detected (high-precision on-disk\n26\t  signal) with a manual **Advance â†’** override. The dashboard tile relabels and migrates from the\n27\t  Research zone to the Plan/Build zone.\n28\t- **SC2 â€” Context-relief handoff.** When the context window gets too full (or you choose), Anchor\n29\t  **warns and offers a one-click handoff** to a fresh session that JOINS the same effort (same\n30\t  tile/lineage), carrying the docs + summary forward via the proven v11.1 machinery. The handoff\n31\t  is the exception, never the default; nothing is auto-submitted on your behalf.\n32\t- **SC3 â€” Layout D dashboard.** Renders the approved Layout D: latest-research headline +\n33\t  collapsible older-research shelf; latest-plan/build headline + collapsible shelf; a persistent\n34\t  right column (Grass + Deliverables); a bottom docked window with **summary on top** and a\n35\t  **full-width, height-resizable terminal**.\n36\t- **SC4 â€” Always durable, no Save button.** Every effort auto-persists per-stage docs + a generated\n37\t  per-stage summary + (for builds) an auto-resolved-or-pinned deliverable. No Save button. A summary\n38\t  is written **before** a session closes. Efforts are reopenable and can seed new efforts.\n39\t- **SC5 â€” Grass workbench.** Grass = the approved two-pane workbench: ONE session per idea (no\n40\t  Research/Plan split), auto-loaded history + deliverable links, no Save button, **Migrate to\n41\t  project â†‘**, âœ• â†’ Boneyard.\n42\t- **SC6 â€” General + Boneyard retained.** General session kept (bare; deliverables linked; summary\n43\t  before close). Per-project Boneyard captures eliminated content.\n44\t- **SC7 â€” Legacy grouped, not rewritten.** Existing researchâ†’planâ†’build chains render AS efforts via\n45\t  a **view-layer grouping** (no stored-record rewrite; self-heals from the registry; rollback =\n46\t  ignore the view). No destructive migration.\n47\t- **SC8 â€” Invariants preserved.** Python stdlib-only (lone `pywinpty` exception); hermetic tests\n48\t  (stub PTY + stub stream-json + temp dirs; never bind `:8777`; never touch real data/network;\n49\t  `ANCHOR_PROACTIVE_SUMMARY` off in tests); Playwright dev-only; `distro.py` scan green (new module\n50\t  added to `dist_manifest.txt`); every UI wave gated by rendered-DOM (pos+neg) + real\n51\t  Playwright/Chromium + screenshot-vs-mockup + John's sign-off; `check_rnd_v12_surface` walks the\n52\t  new surface fully stubbed.\n53\t\n54\t### Non-goals (Grasscatch â€” explicitly OUT)\n55\t\n56\t- No calendar / \"Anchor-as-app\" work (separate efforts).\n57\t- No changes to the trio **skills** themselves (researchPrime / Crucible / Foreman).\n58\t- No change to the git/gh seams (`worktrees._git` / `ANCHOR_GH_CMD`).\n59\t- No multi-user / cloud / auth-model change.\n60\t- No literal \"one Claude context forced through all three skills\" â€” continuity is default but the\n61\t  context-relief handoff exists precisely so context never has to be force-shared.\n62\t- No destructive rewrite of existing session/chain records.\n63\t\n64\t---\n65\t\n66\t## 2. The problem v12 fixes, and the model\n67\t\n68\tThe v6â€“v11.1 model runs the trio as **separate sessions linked by a chain**, with a managed\n69\thandoff between each. Six versions went into making that handoff reliable â€” and it is still the\n70\tsingle most bug-prone seam and awkward in daily use. **But the fix is not to delete the session\n71\tboundary; it is to stop *managing a handoff* at every boundary.**\n72\t\n73\t**Lived-workflow evidence (John, 2026-06-21):** working Râ†’Pâ†’B in one Claude session is natural â€”\n74\tafter research, Claude itself offers to plan; after planning, to build â€” and it does **not** need a\n75\tsilent handoff to do so. The continuity *is* the value, and it already works conversationally.\n76\t\n77\t**The continuity-first model:**\n78\t\n79\t- **Default = one session.** You progress Râ†’Pâ†’B in the same conversation; each skill loads as you\n80\t  go (you or Claude drive it). Anchor does not interrupt.\n81\t- **Advance = relabel + save.** Anchor *observes* the progression (a plan/build doc appears, or you\n82\t  click Advance), **persists + summarizes** the stage just completed, and **migrates the tile** to\n83\t  the next zone. It spawns no session and writes nothing to your PTY.\n84\t- **Handoff = context-relief valve.** Only when the context window fills (or you choose) does Anchor\n85\t  **warn + offer a one-click handoff** to a fresh session that continues the *same effort* â€” reusing\n86\t  the v11.1 `prepare_stage_handoff` machinery (persist docs â†’ real doc-referencing prompt â†’\n87\t  HANDOFF.md/NEXT-PROMPT.md â†’ pending paste, nothing auto-submitted).\n88\t\n89\tThis keeps clean context available *when needed* without throwing away continuity by default, and it\n90\tturns the Shark Tank's BLOCKERs from premise errors into small, named engineering items.\n91\t\n92\t---\n93\t\n94\t## 3. Current architecture (brownfield ground truth â€” Confirmed; file:line verified in Stage-0 ingest)\n95\t\n96\t- **Session record** (`session_registry._normalize`): `session_id, project_id, lane, backend,\n97\t  worktree_path, branch, status, created_at, label, seeded, seed_text, parent_session_id, chain_id,\n98\t  pending_paste, paste_flushed, grass_origin`. Lane effectively immutable after register.\n99\t- **Lanes** (`terminal_session._valid_lanes` / `LANE_SKILL`): trio = research / plan(planning) /\n100\t  build; bare = general, grass. Statusâ†’color: running=green, needs-attention/done=amber, failed=red,\n101\t  idle=grey.\n102\t- **Chains** (`session_registry.chain_for` / `chain_members`, `_CHAIN_LANE_ORDER`): researchâ†’planâ†’\n103\t  build via `parent_session_id` + shared `chain_id`.\n104\t- **Effort storage** (`effort_history.py`): per-lane `<lane>/efforts/<job_id>.pointer.json` +\n105\t  `<lane>/index.json`; **each persisted-doc effort is already tagged with the originating\n106\t  `session_id`** (v8 keystone). `efforts_for_session_id`, `persist_session_docs` (copy+commit a\n107\t  session's produced docs into the main project **before reap**; `_produced_doc_rels` =\n108\t  `git status --porcelain` âˆª `git diff --name-only HEAD` â€” **a whole-worktree diff against the\n109\t  branch base**, âš  the doc-attribution crux), `delete_session_efforts` (drop pointers/summary, keep\n110\t  docs), `FOLD_LANES`.\n111\t- **Lifecycle** (`terminal_session.py`): `start_session` â†’ worktree â†’ bare PTY â†’ register RUNNING â†’\n112\t  seed once. `kill` persists docs â†’ reaps PTY+worktree â†’ Boneyard `killed`. `delete_session`\n113\t  kills-if-live â†’ drops record+efforts (keeps docs) â†’ Boneyard `deleted`. âš  `kill` is the ONLY\n114\t  durable-summary+persist path and it ALSO reaps the worktree.\n115\t- **Auto-advance (the legacy handoff path â€” to be retired for efforts)**:\n116\t  `auto_advance_planning_to_build` (fires for any planning-lane session reaching DONE with no child\n117\t  build â†’ mints a new build session); `reconcile_and_advance` (wired into the `term_sessions`\n118\t  refresh poll); `prepare_stage_handoff` (v11/v11.1); endpoints `/api/rnd/advance_session`,\n119\t  `/api/rnd/finish_to_build`; the `_PROJECT_WINDOW_JS` \"Advance to Planning â†’\" buttons.\n120\t- **Deliverables** (`deliverables.py`): `resolve_build_deliverable` is **session-scoped**, explicit\n121\t  signals only (session product member â†’ pin/marker member â†’ single-build fallback), honest\n122\t  unresolved. `backfill_*`, `launch_deliverable`, `pin_deliverable` (content-addressed, idempotent).\n123\t- **Summaries** (`summarizer.py`): cache keyed by **`(folder, project_id, lane, session_id)`**\n124\t  (`summary_dir`/`load_cached` take `lane`, NOT stage); generate-twice + grounding filter;\n125\t  `SUMMARY_SCHEMA_VERSION=2` heal; `summarize_project`, `session_blurb`, `short_summary_text`,\n126\t  `tile_blurb`, `session_doc_roles`. Render reads cache only.\n127\t- **Boneyard** (`boneyard.py`): per-project content-addressed index; killed/deleted/grass-deleted;\n128\t  capture wired best-effort.\n129\t- **Grass** (`effort_history.py`): idea record `{job_id, status raw/refined/promoted, title, notes,\n130\t  refinements (dev-N), dev_sessions {laneâ†’sid}, exported_to, archives, grass_origin}`;\n131\t  `grass_workbench_data`, `develop_grass_idea`, `export_grass_to_project`, `archive_grass_session`,\n132\t  `advance_grass_research_to_plan`.\n133\t- **Render** (`anchor_gui.py`): `render_project_window_html` (f-string, double-brace) +\n134\t  `_PROJECT_WINDOW_JS` (RAW single-brace) â€” opposite brace rules âš . 5-col `.p2lanes` Kanban;\n135\t  `_gather_project_sessions` merges registry + effort sessions; panel manager\n136\t  (`openPanel`/`minimize`/`maximize`/`closePanel`=close-to-tile vs `killPanel` vs `deletePanel`);\n137\t  xterm mount+fit+ResizeObserver; transport WS `term_ws` â†’ SSE `term_stream2` + POST `term_input2`,\n138\t  token-authed.\n139\t\n140\t**Reuse-over-rewrite insight:** persistence + deliverable + summary + boneyard + the v11.1 handoff\n141\tare already session-tagged and largely fit. v12 adds: (a) stage fields on the record, (b) a\n142\t**per-stage baseline commit** so the existing whole-worktree diff attributes per stage, (c) an\n143\tin-session **relabel-style advance** that retires the legacy auto-advance for efforts, (d) a\n144\t**context-relief handoff** reusing v11.1, (e) an **effort view-layer** grouping chains, and (f) the\n145\tLayout-D render. Only the effort view/migrate helper is a new module.\n146\t\n147\t---\n148\t\n149\t## 4. The v12 design\n150\t\n151\t### 4.1 Effort = a session that carries a stage (extends `session_registry`)\n152\t\n153\tAdd to the normalized record (back-compat defaults in parens; old records normalize with no crash):\n154\t\n155\t- `kind`: `\"trio\" | \"general\" | \"grass-dev\"` (derived from lane on normalize when absent).\n156\t- `current_stage`: `\"\" | \"research\" | \"plan\" | \"build\"` (init from the starting lane; \"\" for non-trio).\n157\t- `stage_history`: append-only `[{stage, store_lane, started_at, ended_at|null, baseline_ref,\n158\t  seeded:bool, summary_ref|null, doc_count}]`. The active stage's entry has `ended_at=null`.\n159\t  **`store_lane` is recorded per stage** so the closed stage's docs/summary resolve under the lane\n160\t  they were written in (fixes the Analyst A1 read-path issue).\n161\t- `seeded_stages`: list (audit).\n162\t- `effort_id`: the effort's stable id = the root session_id (a fresh effort: its own id; a\n163\t  context-relief continuation: the original effort_id, inherited via `start_session(effort_id=â€¦)`).\n164\t- `effort_managed` (bool, default **False**): the v12 discriminator. Set **True** ONLY by the v12\n165\t  entrypoints (the \"+ New effort\" start, `handoff_to_fresh`, `advance_stage`/`finish_stage`). Legacy\n166\t  records â€” including the synthetic projects in the v6/v8/v10/v11 healthcheck walks â€” stay False. **Every\n167\t  retirement gate keys on `effort_managed`, never on `kind`/`current_stage`** (which legacy records also\n168\t  carry), so the legacy walks keep passing unchanged (Shark C3).\n169\t- `lane` is retained as the **current store-lane** (research/planning/build) and flips with\n170\t  `current_stage`. **The board routes by `current_stage`/`kind` only** â€” every `chain_members`/lane\n171\t  sort consumer is audited before lane is made mutable (Skeptic SK-8).\n172\t\n173\t**Board routing (SC1):** a trio effort with `current_stage==\"research\"` â†’ Research headline+shelf;\n174\t`current_stage âˆˆ {plan,build}` â†’ Plan/Build headline+shelf (the tile migrates). `general`/`grass-dev`\n175\tnever appear in the trio zones.\n176\t\n177\t### 4.2 Per-stage baseline commit + stage-scoped persist & summary (fixes F2/SK-2/SK-3/A1/A6)\n178\t\n179\tThe keystone change that makes in-session stages attribute cleanly:\n180\t\n181\t- At each stage **start** (effort start, and each advance), record a **baseline marker** â€” a commit\n182\t  (or tree-ish) in the effort's worktree â€” stored as `baseline_ref` on the stage_history entry.\n183\t- `persist_session_docs` gains a stage-scoped variant. The produced-doc set for a stage is computed\n184\t  with **exact git commands** (Shark B2 â€” \"porcelain since baseline\" is not a real construct):\n185\t  `git diff --name-only <baseline>..HEAD` (committed-since) âˆª `git diff --name-only <baseline> --`\n186\t  (working-tree vs baseline) âˆª `git status --porcelain -uall` additions â€” **minus** paths already\n187\t  attributed to a closed prior stage. Only what THIS stage produced, not everything since the worktree\n188\t  was cut.\n189\t- Persisted efforts are tagged `(session_id, stage)`; add `efforts_for_session_stage`.\n190\t- **Summaries keyed by `(session_id, stage)`**: thread a `stage` arg through\n191\t  `summarize_session`/`load_cached`/`summary_dir`/`session_blurb`/`session_doc_roles`; cache under\n192\t  `<store_lane>/summaries/<session_id>/<stage>/`. Bump `SUMMARY_SCHEMA_VERSION` (stale single-key\n193\t  caches â†’ MISS â†’ heal). The read path resolves a closed stage via its `stage_history.store_lane`.\n194\t- **Deliverable**: `resolve_build_deliverable` **and** `backfill_build_deliverables` (the rescan path â€”\n195\t  Shark C6) are fed ONLY the **build-stage** doc set (filter by the build stage_history entry), so a\n196\t  plan-stage MASTER-PLAN.md can never be mis-resolved/auto-pinned as the build product. Honest\n197\t  unresolved when `current_stage != build` or no signal.\n198\t\n199\t### 4.3 In-session advance = relabel + save (extends `terminal_session`; retires legacy auto-advance)\n200\t\n201\t`advance_stage(session_id, to_stage=None, mode=\"manual\"|\"auto\", project_id=None)`:\n202\t\n203\t1. Take `paths.WRITE_LOCK` (or a per-session lock). Validate live trio effort; `to_stage` is the\n204\t   **next** stage; **idempotent** â€” if `current_stage >= to_stage`, no-op (fixes concurrency A7 /\n205\t   double-advance from a manual+auto race).\n206\t2. **Persist** the current stage's docs (stage-scoped, Â§4.2).\n207\t3. **Schedule** the current stage's summary (background; `summary_ref` on the closing entry).\n208\t4. Close the current stage_history entry (`ended_at`); record the new stage's `baseline_ref`; append\n209\t   the new entry; flip `current_stage` + `lane`.\n210\t5. **No session spawn. No PTY injection.** (Manual mode MAY optionally offer \"load <next skill> for\n211\t   me\" â€” an explicit, opt-in convenience that writes one skill-load turn; it is NOT the default and\n212\t   NOT how the common path works. The default is: you/Claude already moved on; Anchor just relabels.)\n213\t6. The tile migrates zones on next render.\n214\t\n215\t`detect_stage_progress(session_id)` (called from the `term_sessions` refresh): **on-disk\n216\thigh-precision signal only** â€” researchâ†’plan auto-advances only when a committed MASTER-PLAN.md +\n217\tIMPLEMENTATION-PLAN.md pair newer than the stage start appears; planâ†’build only on a committed\n218\tEXECUTION-LOG / build product. **Never** scrapes the PTY for a skill name (avoids the v11.1\n219\tseed-echo false-fire). Conversation-only stages do not auto-advance â€” that's the manual Advance â†’'s\n220\tjob (stated plainly so SC1's auto claim is testable and honest â€” Analyst A5).\n221\t\n222\t**Retirement map (fixes SK-1/A3 + Shark C1/C2/C3/C4 â€” no two advance models):** gated on\n223\t`effort_managed==True` (NOT `kind`), EVERY session-minting path early-returns for an effort:\n224\t`auto_advance_planning_to_build` **and all its call sites** â€” the `term_kill` handler branch (C1), the\n225\t`finish_to_build` handler, and `reconcile_and_advance`; the `/api/rnd/advance_session` +\n226\t`/api/rnd/finish_to_build` handlers; **both** `_PROJECT_WINDOW_JS` advance bars â€” research\n227\t\"Advance to Planning â†’\" AND planning \"Finish â†’ Build â†’\" (C2); and the grass second-advance\n228\t`advance_grass_research_to_plan` + `/api/rnd/grass_advance` + its button (C4). For legacy\n229\t(`effort_managed==False`) records they stay fully live, so the v6/v8/v10/v11.1 healthcheck walks pass\n230\tunchanged (C3). The healthcheck asserts an advanced effort spawns **zero** new sessions (session-id\n231\tset-equality) AND that a legacy record still mints.\n232\t\n233\t`finish_stage` / non-reaping durability (fixes SK-7): factor the persist+summarize keystone out of\n234\t`kill` into a primitive that runs against the live worktree **without reaping** it, so a stage\n235\tboundary (and a \"summary before close\") never tears down the shared worktree. `kill` keeps calling\n236\tit, then reaps.\n237\t\n238\t### 4.4 Context-relief handoff (warn + one-click) + restart recovery (SC2; fixes F6)\n239\t\n240\t- A **context-fullness signal** (token/turn budget heuristic on the live session) raises a UI\n241\t  **warn banner**: \"context getting full â€” hand off to a fresh session?\" One click â†’\n242\t  `handoff_to_fresh(effort_id)`: persist current stage (Â§4.2) â†’ `prepare_stage_handoff` builds the\n243\t  real doc-referencing prompt â†’ start a fresh session that **inherits `effort_id`** (joins the same\n244\t  effort/tile/lineage) with the prompt as a **pending paste** (v11.1; nothing auto-submitted). The\n245\t  old session is marked done-stage; the effort continues. Auto and manual-only are NOT chosen\n246\t  (decision: warn + one-click).\n247\t- **Restart recovery:** on boot, an effort whose registry record is RUNNING but whose PTY is gone â†’\n248\t  persist whatever the active stage's worktree holds, mark the stage **interrupted** (not DONE),\n249\t  keep it reopenable to **continue the same stage** (a fresh session inheriting `effort_id`). A crash\n250\t  is not a \"close\"; SC4's summary-before-close fires on the orderly close + on this recovery persist.\n251\t\n252\t### 4.5 Effort view-layer â€” group chains into efforts (NEW `effort_view.py`; fixes F4/SK-6/A4, SC7)\n253\t\n254\t`build_effort_view(folder, project_id)` groups the project's registry records by `chain_id` and\n255\treturns ONE effort per chain **at render time** (a derived VIEW, not a stored rewrite):\n256\t\n257\t- `effort_id` = chain root session_id; `stage_history` synthesized from the chain members (each\n258\t  member = one stage, referencing its already-persisted docs + cached summary); `current_stage` =\n259\t  most-advanced member; `status` from the newest member; live worktree if a member is running.\n260\t- New v12 efforts (single session carrying stages) are already efforts; legacy chains are *grouped*\n261\t  into the same shape â€” uniform render.\n262\t- **Self-healing & drift-safe:** the view is **rebuilt from the registry on every render/rescan**\n263\t  (a cache, never a source of truth). A member deleted from the registry simply drops from the view\n264\t  (no ghost stage). No `efforts.json` source-of-truth; rollback = stop calling the view. Idempotent.\n265\t  Guarded like v9 `project_move` (never the Anchor repo; reads, never reaps, live members).\n266\t- Deduped so a migrated chain + a new live session render the effort **exactly once** (no double\n267\t  tiles â€” Skeptic SK-6).\n268\t\n269\t### 4.6 Layout D dashboard (rebuild `render_project_window_html` + `_PROJECT_WINDOW_JS`)\n270\t\n271\tPer `_mockups/dashboard_D_headline_shelf.html`: Latest-Research headline + collapsible shelf;\n272\tLatest-Plan/Build headline + collapsible shelf; persistent right column (Grass + Deliverables); a\n273\t**single bottom docked window** (replaces the floating panel stack): title bar (stage track +\n274\tmin/max/close + distinct **Kill â†’ Boneyard** + the context-full warn banner + **Advance â†’**),\n275\t**summary on top (full width)**, a **draggable vertical splitter**, then a **full-width terminal\n276\twhose height the user drags**. Selecting any headline/little-tile opens it here. A **+ New effort**\n277\taffordance starts an effort at research (or plan) â€” stated explicitly (fixes F7).\n278\t\n279\t**Reuse:** transport (`term_ws`/`term_stream2`/`term_input2`), xterm mount/fit/observer (with a\n280\t**debounced** splitter-drag fit â€” SK-9), `_renderSplitSummary`/`_loadPanelSummary`, status-light\n281\tclasses, token auth, masthead + lifecycle + GitHub controls. **Rewrite:** 5-col grid â†’ headline+\n282\tshelf; floating stack â†’ single dock; split â†’ summary-top / terminal-bottom. A **render-smoke test**\n283\t(import + non-empty balanced-brace HTML) runs BEFORE the Playwright wave so the f-string/RAW-string\n284\tboundary fails fast (A9).\n285\t\n286\t**Engine note (F7):** Gemini is research-only. An effort started on Gemini that advances past\n287\tresearch either blocks the advance with an honest message, or (if the user opts in) the\n288\tcontext-relief/skill-load path relaunches on Claude â€” a documented, explicit exception, never\n289\tsilent.\n290\t\n291\t### 4.7 Grass two-pane workbench (extend `effort_history` grass + render; SC5)\n292\t\n293\tPer `_mockups/grass_2_workbench.html`: left = idea list (capture, search, filter, âœ•â†’Boneyard);\n294\tright = the selected idea's workbench (header with auto-saved indicator + **Migrate to project â†‘** +\n295\tArchive snapshot; idea text; auto-gathered History; **ONE session** with engine toggle + one\n296\tterminal â€” no Research/Plan buttons). Collapse the per-(idea,lane) `dev_sessions` map into a single\n297\tstage-carrying dev session (reuse Â§4.3 advance within grass). **Back-compat:** an existing idea with\n298\ttwo dev_sessions renders the most-advanced as the single workbench session with a stage history; no\n299\torphan; âœ•/Migrate still work (fixes A10). Migrate = `export_grass_to_project` (copy up, idea stays,\n300\t`grass_origin`). âœ• = `delete_grass_idea` â†’ Boneyard.\n301\t\n302\t### 4.8 General + Boneyard (SC6)\n303\t\n304\tGeneral session unchanged (bare lane, summary-before-close, deliverables linked). Boneyard unchanged\n305\t(per-project; killing/deleting an effort or idea files its content). Both surfaced in the Layout-D\n306\tchrome.\n307\t\n308\t---\n309\t\n310\t## 5. Phasing (waves detailed in IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN.md)\n311\t\n312\t- **Phase A â€” Effort backbone:** record stage fields + back-compat normalize; board routing by stage.\n313\t- **Phase B â€” Keystone fix:** per-stage baseline commit + stage-scoped persist/summary/deliverable.\n314\t- **Phase C â€” In-session advance:** `advance_stage` (relabel+save) + `detect_stage_progress` +\n315\t  retirement map + `finish_stage` non-reaping durability + concurrency lock.\n316\t- **Phase D â€” Context-relief handoff + restart recovery.**\n317\t- **Phase E â€” Effort view-layer** (group chains; drift-safe) + deliverable resolve/pin.\n318\t- **Phase F â€” Layout D UI** (headline+shelves+right column; then the bottom dock). [UI-gated]\n319\t- **Phase G â€” Grass workbench + General + Boneyard UI.** [UI-gated]\n320\t- **Phase H â€” Wire-to-live + hardening:** dashboard rows; CLI mirror; `check_rnd_v12_surface`\n321\t  (fully stubbed); distro scan; docs/CLAUDE.md/memory/SESSION-HANDOFF.\n322\t\n323\tUI (the approved Layout D + grass) ships **early** on the chosen backbone (John's sequencing pick),\n324\tnot gated behind the riskier core.\n325\t\n326\t---\n327\t\n328\t## 6. Risks & mitigations (post-Shark)\n329\t\n330\t- **R1 â€” Doc mis-attribution across stages (BLOCKER, confirmed SK-2/F2).** *Mitigation:* per-stage\n331\t  baseline commit + stage-scoped diff (Â§4.2); `efforts_for_session_stage`; healthcheck asserts each\n332\t  stage's persisted set = only that stage's files.\n333\t- **R2 â€” Summary cache mis-key across stages (BLOCKER, SK-3/A1).** *Mitigation:* `(session, stage)`\n334\t  key + per-stage dir + `store_lane` read-resolution; bump schema version; heal stale caches.\n335\t- **R3 â€” Legacy auto-advance spawns sessions for an effort (BLOCKER, SK-1/A3).** *Mitigation:* the\n336\t  Â§4.3 retirement map gates off every legacy advance path for efforts; healthcheck asserts zero new\n337\t  sessions on advance + negative-DOM asserts the old buttons are gone.\n338\t- **R4 â€” Migration split-brain / stale index (MAJOR Ã—3, F4/SK-6/A4).** *Mitigation:* the Â§4.5 view\n339\t  is rebuilt-from-registry each render (a cache, not a source); drift-safe; deduped; rollback = stop\n340\t  calling it.\n341\t- **R5 â€” Context pollution degrades a skill (Contrarian F1).** *Status:* downgraded by John's\n342\t  lived-workflow evidence; *mitigation:* the context-relief handoff (Â§4.4) gives clean context\n343\t  whenever it's actually wanted, so context is never force-shared.\n344\t- **R6 â€” Re-seeding a live PTY is unproven (SK-4/A2).** *Mitigation:* the default advance injects\n345\t  NOTHING into the PTY (relabel+save only); the only PTY-writing path is the v11.1 handoff into a\n346\t  FRESH session (already proven) + the opt-in \"load skill for me\" convenience, both flush-after-greet\n347\t  with the v11.1 base-count guard captured from a re-seed cursor.\n348\t- **R7 â€” Foreman builds in a dirty shared worktree (F3).** *Mitigation:* per-stage baseline commits\n349\t  leave the tree in a clean committed state at build start; if a build needs a pristine checkout the\n350\t  context-relief handoff gives it one. Validated in the healthcheck build walk.\n351\t- **R8 â€” Restart mid-effort loses work (F6).** *Mitigation:* Â§4.4 restart recovery â€” persist active\n352\t  stage, mark interrupted (not DONE), reopenable to continue.\n353\t- **R9 â€” Concurrency: manual+auto advance race / advance-during-input (A7).** *Mitigation:* WRITE_LOCK\n354\t  + idempotency guard in `advance_stage`; both manual and auto go through it.\n355\t- **R10 â€” \"UI looks done but isn't\" + the f-string/RAW brace hazard (A9, the v4 lesson).**\n356\t  *Mitigation:* render-smoke (balanced-brace import) before Playwright; every UI wave gated by DOM\n357\t  pos+neg + Playwright/Chromium + screenshot-vs-mockup + John's sign-off. String-grep-only = HALT.\n358\t- **R11 â€” Grass two-session ideas break under the one-session model (A10).** *Mitigation:* Â§4.7\n359\t  back-compat render + test.\n360\t- **R12 â€” Scope (F5).** *Mitigation:* inclusion test (every wave â†’ an SC); UI ships early decoupled\n361\t  from the core; reuse-over-rewrite is a hard rule.\n362\t\n363\t---\n364\t\n365\t## 7. Done-when (Master-Plan level)\n366\t\n367\tOn a real project: start an effort, work in research, **Advance â†’** (or auto on a committed plan\n368\tset) keeps the SAME session and migrates the tile to Plan/Build while persisting+summarizing the\n369\tresearch stage; each stage's docs attribute only to that stage; a build resolves (or you pin) a\n370\tdeliverable from build-stage docs only; when context fills, a one-click handoff continues the same\n371\teffort in a fresh session; a service restart mid-effort recovers without loss; existing chains render\n372\tas efforts with no double tiles and no destructive rewrite; the Layout-D dashboard + bottom dock +\n373\tgrass workbench match the approved mockups; and `check_rnd_v12_surface` is GREEN fully stubbed â€” all\n374\tinvariants intact, merged only after your per-UI-wave sign-off.\n375\t\n376\t---\n377\t\n378\t## Appendix â€” Shark-Tank Round 1 (2026-06-21)\n379\t\n380\t3 fresh-context Sharks (Skeptic / Contrarian / Analyst), each prompted to refute. **All 3 verdicts:\n381\tBLOCK.** â‰¥2-agree BLOCKERs: doc-attribution in a shared worktree (SK-2+F2); summary cache key across\n382\tstages (SK-3+A1); legacy auto-advance / orphaned advance endpoints spawn sessions (SK-1+A3). 3-way\n383\tMAJOR: migration split-brain (F4+SK-6+A4). Premise challenge (F1, context pollution) **resolved by\n384\tJohn's lived-workflow evidence** â†’ the continuity-first model with a context-relief handoff, which\n385\tconverts every BLOCKER into a named, testable engineering item folded into Â§4/Â§6 above. Convergence\n386\tauthority: John (locked the revised model + sequencing 2026-06-21).\n387\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8f450d41-5be0-4cae-820d-1931879d0eb6","uuid":"84cfb4a2-843d-438c-b104-0870300d5eb2","timestamp":"2026-06-23T00:49:18.823Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\dev\\Anchor\\planning\\rnd-v12\\MASTER-PLAN.md","content":"# Anchor R&D Surface v12 â€” \"Efforts\" (continuity-first single-session trio) Â· MASTER PLAN\n\n> **Status:** Stage 1 (Master Plan) â€” REVISED after Shark-Tank Round 1 (all 3 Sharks BLOCKed the\n> first \"literally one shared session/worktree/context\" draft; John's lived-workflow evidence\n> reframed the model to **continuity-first with a context-relief handoff**). Approved by John for\n> the model + sequencing 2026-06-21. Frozen design lives here; the wave-by-wave build plan lives in\n> `IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN.md`. Approved mockups: `_mockups/dashboard_D_headline_shelf.html` (dashboard)\n> + `_mockups/grass_2_workbench.html` (grass catcher).\n\n---\n\n## 1. North Star (LOCKED 2026-06-21)\n\n> **Anchor's per-project dashboard lets John run a unit of work as a single continuous \"effort\"\n> that flows Research â†’ Plan â†’ Build in ONE session by default â€” the stage transition is a\n> lightweight relabel, not a managed handoff â€” with a fresh-session handoff only as a\n> context-relief valve, and with every effort's docs, deliverable, and summary durably saved and\n> reopenable, surfaced on the simple Layout-D dashboard.**\n\n### Success criteria (each testable)\n\n- **SC1 â€” Continuity-first in-session stages.** An effort is ONE session by default; you work\n  Râ†’Pâ†’B in the same conversation, each skill loading as the work naturally progresses. \"Advance\"\n  is a **relabel + persist + summarize** of the completed stage â€” it spawns **no new session** and\n  injects **nothing** into your conversation. Advance is auto-detected (high-precision on-disk\n  signal) with a manual **Advance â†’** override. The dashboard tile relabels and migrates from the\n  Research zone to the Plan/Build zone.\n- **SC2 â€” Context-relief handoff.** When the context window gets too full (or you choose), Anchor\n  **warns and offers a one-click handoff** to a fresh session that JOINS the same effort (same\n  tile/lineage), carrying the docs + summary forward via the proven v11.1 machinery. The handoff\n  is the exception, never the default; nothing is auto-submitted on your behalf.\n- **SC3 â€” Layout D dashboard.** Renders the approved Layout D: latest-research headline +\n  collapsible older-research shelf; latest-plan/build headline + collapsible shelf; a persistent\n  right column (Grass + Deliverables); a bottom docked window with **summary on top** and a\n  **full-width, height-resizable terminal**.\n- **SC4 â€” Always durable, no Save button.** Every effort auto-persists per-stage docs + a generated\n  per-stage summary + (for builds) an auto-resolved-or-pinned deliverable. No Save button. A summary\n  is written **before** a session closes. Efforts are reopenable and can seed new efforts.\n- **SC5 â€” Grass workbench.** Grass = the approved two-pane workbench: ONE session per idea (no\n  Research/Plan split), auto-loaded history + deliverable links, no Save button, **Migrate to\n  project â†‘**, âœ• â†’ Boneyard.\n- **SC6 â€” General + Boneyard retained.** General session kept (bare; deliverables linked; summary\n  before close). Per-project Boneyard captures eliminated content.\n- **SC7 â€” Legacy grouped, not rewritten.** Existing researchâ†’planâ†’build chains render AS efforts via\n  a **view-layer grouping** (no stored-record rewrite; self-heals from the registry; rollback =\n  ignore the view). No destructive migration.\n- **SC8 â€” Invariants preserved.** Python stdlib-only (lone `pywinpty` exception); hermetic tests\n  (stub PTY + stub stream-json + temp dirs; never bind `:8777`; never touch real data/network;\n  `ANCHOR_PROACTIVE_SUMMARY` off in tests); Playwright dev-only; `distro.py` scan green (new module\n  added to `dist_manifest.txt`); every UI wave gated by rendered-DOM (pos+neg) + real\n  Playwright/Chromium + screenshot-vs-mockup + John's sign-off; `check_rnd_v12_surface` walks the\n  new surface fully stubbed.\n\n### Non-goals (Grasscatch â€” explicitly OUT)\n\n- No calendar / \"Anchor-as-app\" work (separate efforts).\n- No changes to the trio **skills** themselves (researchPrime / Crucible / Foreman).\n- No change to the git/gh seams (`worktrees._git` / `ANCHOR_GH_CMD`).\n- No multi-user / cloud / auth-model change.\n- No literal \"one Claude context forced through all three skills\" â€” continuity is default but the\n  context-relief handoff exists precisely so context never has to be force-shared.\n- No destructive rewrite of existing session/chain records.\n\n---\n\n## 2. The problem v12 fixes, and the model\n\nThe v6â€“v11.1 model runs the trio as **separate sessions linked by a chain**, with a managed\nhandoff between each. Six versions went into making that handoff reliable â€” and it is still the\nsingle most bug-prone seam and awkward in daily use. **But the fix is not to delete the session\nboundary; it is to stop *managing a handoff* at every boundary.**\n\n**Lived-workflow evidence (John, 2026-06-21):** working Râ†’Pâ†’B in one Claude session is natural â€”\nafter research, Claude itself offers to plan; after planning, to build â€” and it does **not** need a\nsilent handoff to do so. The continuity *is* the value, and it already works conversationally.\n\n**The continuity-first model:**\n\n- **Default = one session.** You progress Râ†’Pâ†’B in the same conversation; each skill loads as you\n  go (you or Claude drive it). Anchor does not interrupt.\n- **Advance = relabel + save.** Anchor *observes* the progression (a plan/build doc appears, or you\n  click Advance), **persists + summarizes** the stage just completed, and **migrates the tile** to\n  the next zone. It spawns no session and writes nothing to your PTY.\n- **Handoff = context-relief valve.** Only when the context window fills (or you choose) does Anchor\n  **warn + offer a one-click handoff** to a fresh session that continues the *same effort* â€” reusing\n  the v11.1 `prepare_stage_handoff` machinery (persist docs â†’ real doc-referencing prompt â†’\n  HANDOFF.md/NEXT-PROMPT.md â†’ pending paste, nothing auto-submitted).\n\nThis keeps clean context available *when needed* without throwing away continuity by default, and it\nturns the Shark Tank's BLOCKERs from premise errors into small, named engineering items.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Current architecture (brownfield ground truth â€” Confirmed; file:line verified in Stage-0 ingest)\n\n- **Session record** (`session_registry._normalize`): `session_id, project_id, lane, backend,\n  worktree_path, branch, status, created_at, label, seeded, seed_text, parent_session_id, chain_id,\n  pending_paste, paste_flushed, grass_origin`. Lane effectively immutable after register.\n- **Lanes** (`terminal_session._valid_lanes` / `LANE_SKILL`): trio = research / plan(planning) /\n  build; bare = general, grass. Statusâ†’color: running=green, needs-attention/done=amber, failed=red,\n  idle=grey.\n- **Chains** (`session_registry.chain_for` / `chain_members`, `_CHAIN_LANE_ORDER`): researchâ†’planâ†’\n  build via `parent_session_id` + shared `chain_id`.\n- **Effort storage** (`effort_history.py`): per-lane `<lane>/efforts/<job_id>.pointer.json` +\n  `<lane>/index.json`; **each persisted-doc effort is already tagged with the originating\n  `session_id`** (v8 keystone). `efforts_for_session_id`, `persist_session_docs` (copy+commit a\n  session's produced docs into the main project **before reap**; `_produced_doc_rels` =\n  `git status --porcelain` âˆª `git diff --name-only HEAD` â€” **a whole-worktree diff against the\n  branch base**, âš  the doc-attribution crux), `delete_session_efforts` (drop pointers/summary, keep\n  docs), `FOLD_LANES`.\n- **Lifecycle** (`terminal_session.py`): `start_session` â†’ worktree â†’ bare PTY â†’ register RUNNING â†’\n  seed once. `kill` persists docs â†’ reaps PTY+worktree â†’ Boneyard `killed`. `delete_session`\n  kills-if-live â†’ drops record+efforts (keeps docs) â†’ Boneyard `deleted`. âš  `kill` is the ONLY\n  durable-summary+persist path and it ALSO reaps the worktree.\n- **Auto-advance (the legacy handoff path â€” to be retired for efforts)**:\n  `auto_advance_planning_to_build` (fires for any planning-lane session reaching DONE with no child\n  build â†’ mints a new build session); `reconcile_and_advance` (wired into the `term_sessions`\n  refresh poll); `prepare_stage_handoff` (v11/v11.1); endpoints `/api/rnd/advance_session`,\n  `/api/rnd/finish_to_build`; the `_PROJECT_WINDOW_JS` \"Advance to Planning â†’\" buttons.\n- **Deliverables** (`deliverables.py`): `resolve_build_deliverable` is **session-scoped**, explicit\n  signals only (session product member â†’ pin/marker member â†’ single-build fallback), honest\n  unresolved. `backfill_*`, `launch_deliverable`, `pin_deliverable` (content-addressed, idempotent).\n- **Summaries** (`summarizer.py`): cache keyed by **`(folder, project_id, lane, session_id)`**\n  (`summary_dir`/`load_cached` take `lane`, NOT stage); generate-twice + grounding filter;\n  `SUMMARY_SCHEMA_VERSION=2` heal; `summarize_project`, `session_blurb`, `short_summary_text`,\n  `tile_blurb`, `session_doc_roles`. Render reads cache only.\n- **Boneyard** (`boneyard.py`): per-project content-addressed index; killed/deleted/grass-deleted;\n  capture wired best-effort.\n- **Grass** (`effort_history.py`): idea record `{job_id, status raw/refined/promoted, title, notes,\n  refinements (dev-N), dev_sessions {laneâ†’sid}, exported_to, archives, grass_origin}`;\n  `grass_workbench_data`, `develop_grass_idea`, `export_grass_to_project`, `archive_grass_session`,\n  `advance_grass_research_to_plan`.\n- **Render** (`anchor_gui.py`): `render_project_window_html` (f-string, double-brace) +\n  `_PROJECT_WINDOW_JS` (RAW single-brace) â€” opposite brace rules âš . 5-col `.p2lanes` Kanban;\n  `_gather_project_sessions` merges registry + effort sessions; panel manager\n  (`openPanel`/`minimize`/`maximize`/`closePanel`=close-to-tile vs `killPanel` vs `deletePanel`);\n  xterm mount+fit+ResizeObserver; transport WS `term_ws` â†’ SSE `term_stream2` + POST `term_input2`,\n  token-authed.\n\n**Reuse-over-rewrite insight:** persistence + deliverable + summary + boneyard + the v11.1 handoff\nare already session-tagged and largely fit. v12 adds: (a) stage fields on the record, (b) a\n**per-stage baseline commit** so the existing whole-worktree diff attributes per stage, (c) an\nin-session **relabel-style advance** that retires the legacy auto-advance for efforts, (d) a\n**context-relief handoff** reusing v11.1, (e) an **effort view-layer** grouping chains, and (f) the\nLayout-D render. Only the effort view/migrate helper is a new module.\n\n---\n\n## 4. The v12 design\n\n### 4.1 Effort = a session that carries a stage (extends `session_registry`)\n\nAdd to the normalized record (back-compat defaults in parens; old records normalize with no crash):\n\n- `kind`: `\"trio\" | \"general\" | \"grass-dev\"` (derived from lane on normalize when absent).\n- `current_stage`: `\"\" | \"research\" | \"plan\" | \"build\"` (init from the starting lane; \"\" for non-trio).\n- `stage_history`: append-only `[{stage, store_lane, started_at, ended_at|null, baseline_ref,\n  seeded:bool, summary_ref|null, doc_count}]`. The active stage's entry has `ended_at=null`.\n  **`store_lane` is recorded per stage** so the closed stage's docs/summary resolve under the lane\n  they were written in (fixes the Analyst A1 read-path issue).\n- `seeded_stages`: list (audit).\n- `effort_id`: the effort's stable id = the root session_id (a fresh effort: its own id; a\n  context-relief continuation: the original effort_id, inherited via `start_session(effort_id=â€¦)`).\n- `effort_managed` (bool, default **False**): the v12 discriminator. Set **True** ONLY by the v12\n  entrypoints (the \"+ New effort\" start, `handoff_to_fresh`, `advance_stage`/`finish_stage`). Legacy\n  records â€” including the synthetic projects in the v6/v8/v10/v11 healthcheck walks â€” stay False. **Every\n  retirement gate keys on `effort_managed`, never on `kind`/`current_stage`** (which legacy records also\n  carry), so the legacy walks keep passing unchanged (Shark C3).\n- `lane` is retained as the **current store-lane** (research/planning/build) and flips with\n  `current_stage`. **The board routes by `current_stage`/`kind` only** â€” every `chain_members`/lane\n  sort consumer is audited before lane is made mutable (Skeptic SK-8).\n\n**Board routing (SC1):** a trio effort with `current_stage==\"research\"` â†’ Research headline+shelf;\n`current_stage âˆˆ {plan,build}` â†’ Plan/Build headline+shelf (the tile migrates). `general`/`grass-dev`\nnever appear in the trio zones.\n\n### 4.2 Per-stage baseline commit + stage-scoped persist & summary (fixes F2/SK-2/SK-3/A1/A6)\n\nThe keystone change that makes in-session stages attribute cleanly:\n\n- At each stage **start** (effort start, and each advance), record a **baseline marker** â€” a commit\n  (or tree-ish) in the effort's worktree â€” stored as `baseline_ref` on the stage_history entry.\n- `persist_session_docs` gains a stage-scoped variant. The produced-doc set for a stage is computed\n  with **exact git commands** (Shark B2 â€” \"porcelain since baseline\" is not a real construct):\n  `git diff --name-only <baseline>..HEAD` (committed-since) âˆª `git diff --name-only <baseline> --`\n  (working-tree vs baseline) âˆª `git status --porcelain -uall` additions â€” **minus** paths already\n  attributed to a closed prior stage. Only what THIS stage produced, not everything since the worktree\n  was cut.\n- Persisted efforts are tagged `(session_id, stage)`; add `efforts_for_session_stage`.\n- **Summaries keyed by `(session_id, stage)`**: thread a `stage` arg through\n  `summarize_session`/`load_cached`/`summary_dir`/`session_blurb`/`session_doc_roles`; cache under\n  `<store_lane>/summaries/<session_id>/<stage>/`. Bump `SUMMARY_SCHEMA_VERSION` (stale single-key\n  caches â†’ MISS â†’ heal). The read path resolves a closed stage via its `stage_history.store_lane`.\n- **Deliverable**: `resolve_build_deliverable` **and** `backfill_build_deliverables` (the rescan path â€”\n  Shark C6) are fed ONLY the **build-stage** doc set (filter by the build stage_history entry), so a\n  plan-stage MASTER-PLAN.md can never be mis-resolved/auto-pinned as the build product. Honest\n  unresolved when `current_stage != build` or no signal.\n\n### 4.3 In-session advance = relabel + save (extends `terminal_session`; retires legacy auto-advance)\n\n`advance_stage(session_id, to_stage=None, mode=\"manual\"|\"auto\", project_id=None)`:\n\n1. Take `paths.WRITE_LOCK` (or a per-session lock). Validate live trio effort; `to_stage` is the\n   **next** stage; **idempotent** â€” if `current_stage >= to_stage`, no-op (fixes concurrency A7 /\n   double-advance from a manual+auto race).\n2. **Persist** the current stage's docs (stage-scoped, Â§4.2).\n3. **Schedule** the current stage's summary (background; `summary_ref` on the closing entry).\n4. Close the current stage_history entry (`ended_at`); record the new stage's `baseline_ref`; append\n   the new entry; flip `current_stage` + `lane`.\n5. **No session spawn. No PTY injection.** (Manual mode MAY optionally offer \"load <next skill> for\n   me\" â€” an explicit, opt-in convenience that writes one skill-load turn; it is NOT the default and\n   NOT how the common path works. The default is: you/Claude already moved on; Anchor just relabels.)\n6. The tile migrates zones on next render.\n\n`detect_stage_progress(session_id)` (called from the `term_sessions` refresh): **on-disk\nhigh-precision signal only** â€” researchâ†’plan auto-advances only when a committed MASTER-PLAN.md +\nIMPLEMENTATION-PLAN.md pair newer than the stage start appears; planâ†’build only on a committed\nEXECUTION-LOG / build product. **Never** scrapes the PTY for a skill name (avoids the v11.1\nseed-echo false-fire). Conversation-only stages do not auto-advance â€” that's the manual Advance â†’'s\njob (stated plainly so SC1's auto claim is testable and honest â€” Analyst A5).\n\n**Retirement map (fixes SK-1/A3 + Shark C1/C2/C3/C4 â€” no two advance models):** gated on\n`effort_managed==True` (NOT `kind`), EVERY session-minting path early-returns for an effort:\n`auto_advance_planning_to_build` **and all its call sites** â€” the `term_kill` handler branch (C1), the\n`finish_to_build` handler, and `reconcile_and_advance`; the `/api/rnd/advance_session` +\n`/api/rnd/finish_to_build` handlers; **both** `_PROJECT_WINDOW_JS` advance bars â€” research\n\"Advance to Planning â†’\" AND planning \"Finish â†’ Build â†’\" (C2); and the grass second-advance\n`advance_grass_research_to_plan` + `/api/rnd/grass_advance` + its button (C4). For legacy\n(`effort_managed==False`) records they stay fully live, so the v6/v8/v10/v11.1 healthcheck walks pass\nunchanged (C3). The healthcheck asserts an advanced effort spawns **zero** new sessions (session-id\nset-equality) AND that a legacy record still mints.\n\n`finish_stage` / non-reaping durability (fixes SK-7): factor the persist+summarize keystone out of\n`kill` into a primitive that runs against the live worktree **without reaping** it, so a stage\nboundary (and a \"summary before close\") never tears down the shared worktree. `kill` keeps calling\nit, then reaps.\n\n### 4.4 Context-relief handoff (warn + one-click) + restart recovery (SC2; fixes F6)\n\n- A **context-fullness signal** (token/turn budget heuristic on the live session) raises a UI\n  **warn banner**: \"context getting full â€” hand off to a fresh session?\" One click â†’\n  `handoff_to_fresh(effort_id)`: persist current stage (Â§4.2) â†’ `prepare_stage_handoff` builds the\n  real doc-referencing prompt â†’ start a fresh session that **inherits `effort_id`** (joins the same\n  effort/tile/lineage) with the prompt as a **pending paste** (v11.1; nothing auto-submitted). The\n  old session is marked done-stage; the effort continues. Auto and manual-only are NOT chosen\n  (decision: warn + one-click).\n- **Restart recovery:** on boot, an effort whose registry record is RUNNING but whose PTY is gone â†’\n  persist whatever the active stage's worktree holds, mark the stage **interrupted** (not DONE),\n  keep it reopenable to **continue the same stage** (a fresh session inheriting `effort_id`). A crash\n  is not a \"close\"; SC4's summary-before-close fires on the orderly close + on this recovery persist.\n\n### 4.5 Effort view-layer â€” group chains into efforts (NEW `effort_view.py`; fixes F4/SK-6/A4, SC7)\n\n`build_effort_view(folder, project_id)` groups the project's registry records by `chain_id` and\nreturns ONE effort per chain **at render time** (a derived VIEW, not a stored rewrite):\n\n- `effort_id` = chain root session_id; `stage_history` synthesized from the chain members (each\n  member = one stage, referencing its already-persisted docs + cached summary); `current_stage` =\n  most-advanced member; `status` from the newest member; live worktree if a member is running.\n- New v12 efforts (single session carrying stages) are already efforts; legacy chains are *grouped*\n  into the same shape â€” uniform render.\n- **Self-healing & drift-safe:** the view is **rebuilt from the registry on every render/rescan**\n  (a cache, never a source of truth). A member deleted from the registry simply drops from the view\n  (no ghost stage). No `efforts.json` source-of-truth; rollback = stop calling the view. Idempotent.\n  Guarded like v9 `project_move` (never the Anchor repo; reads, never reaps, live members).\n- Deduped so a migrated chain + a new live session render the effort **exactly once** (no double\n  tiles â€” Skeptic SK-6).\n\n### 4.6 Layout D dashboard (rebuild `render_project_window_html` + `_PROJECT_WINDOW_JS`)\n\nPer `_mockups/dashboard_D_headline_shelf.html`: Latest-Research headline + collapsible shelf;\nLatest-Plan/Build headline + collapsible shelf; persistent right column (Grass + Deliverables); a\n**single bottom docked window** (replaces the floating panel stack): title bar (stage track +\nmin/max/close + distinct **Kill â†’ Boneyard** + the context-full warn banner + **Advance â†’**),\n**summary on top (full width)**, a **draggable vertical splitter**, then a **full-width terminal\nwhose height the user drags**. Selecting any headline/little-tile opens it here. A **+ New effort**\naffordance starts an effort at research (or plan) â€” stated explicitly (fixes F7).\n\n**Reuse:** transport (`term_ws`/`term_stream2`/`term_input2`), xterm mount/fit/observer (with a\n**debounced** splitter-drag fit â€” SK-9), `_renderSplitSummary`/`_loadPanelSummary`, status-light\nclasses, token auth, masthead + lifecycle + GitHub controls. **Rewrite:** 5-col grid â†’ headline+\nshelf; floating stack â†’ single dock; split â†’ summary-top / terminal-bottom. A **render-smoke test**\n(import + non-empty balanced-brace HTML) runs BEFORE the Playwright wave so the f-string/RAW-string\nboundary fails fast (A9).\n\n**Engine note (F7):** Gemini is research-only. An effort started on Gemini that advances past\nresearch either blocks the advance with an honest message, or (if the user opts in) the\ncontext-relief/skill-load path relaunches on Claude â€” a documented, explicit exception, never\nsilent.\n\n### 4.7 Grass two-pane workbench (extend `effort_history` grass + render; SC5)\n\nPer `_mockups/grass_2_workbench.html`: left = idea list (capture, search, filter, âœ•â†’Boneyard);\nright = the selected idea's workbench (header with auto-saved indicator + **Migrate to project â†‘** +\nArchive snapshot; idea text; auto-gathered History; **ONE session** with engine toggle + one\nterminal â€” no Research/Plan buttons). Collapse the per-(idea,lane) `dev_sessions` map into a single\nstage-carrying dev session (reuse Â§4.3 advance within grass). **Back-compat:** an existing idea with\ntwo dev_sessions renders the most-advanced as the single workbench session with a stage history; no\norphan; âœ•/Migrate still work (fixes A10). Migrate = `export_grass_to_project` (copy up, idea stays,\n`grass_origin`). âœ• = `delete_grass_idea` â†’ Boneyard.\n\n### 4.8 General + Boneyard (SC6)\n\nGeneral session unchanged (bare lane, summary-before-close, deliverables linked). Boneyard unchanged\n(per-project; killing/deleting an effort or idea files its content). Both surfaced in the Layout-D\nchrome.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Phasing (waves detailed in IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN.md)\n\n- **Phase A â€” Effort backbone:** record stage fields + back-compat normalize; board routing by stage.\n- **Phase B â€” Keystone fix:** per-stage baseline commit + stage-scoped persist/summary/deliverable.\n- **Phase C â€” In-session advance:** `advance_stage` (relabel+save) + `detect_stage_progress` +\n  retirement map + `finish_stage` non-reaping durability + concurrency lock.\n- **Phase D â€” Context-relief handoff + restart recovery.**\n- **Phase E â€” Effort view-layer** (group chains; drift-safe) + deliverable resolve/pin.\n- **Phase F â€” Layout D UI** (headline+shelves+right column; then the bottom dock). [UI-gated]\n- **Phase G â€” Grass workbench + General + Boneyard UI.** [UI-gated]\n- **Phase H â€” Wire-to-live + hardening:** dashboard rows; CLI mirror; `check_rnd_v12_surface`\n  (fully stubbed); distro scan; docs/CLAUDE.md/memory/SESSION-HANDOFF.\n\nUI (the approved Layout D + grass) ships **early** on the chosen backbone (John's sequencing pick),\nnot gated behind the riskier core.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Risks & mitigations (post-Shark)\n\n- **R1 â€” Doc mis-attribution across stages (BLOCKER, confirmed SK-2/F2).** *Mitigation:* per-stage\n  baseline commit + stage-scoped diff (Â§4.2); `efforts_for_session_stage`; healthcheck asserts each\n  stage's persisted set = only that stage's files.\n- **R2 â€” Summary cache mis-key across stages (BLOCKER, SK-3/A1).** *Mitigation:* `(session, stage)`\n  key + per-stage dir + `store_lane` read-resolution; bump schema version; heal stale caches.\n- **R3 â€” Legacy auto-advance spawns sessions for an effort (BLOCKER, SK-1/A3).** *Mitigation:* the\n  Â§4.3 retirement map gates off every legacy advance path for efforts; healthcheck asserts zero new\n  sessions on advance + negative-DOM asserts the old buttons are gone.\n- **R4 â€” Migration split-brain / stale index (MAJOR Ã—3, F4/SK-6/A4).** *Mitigation:* the Â§4.5 view\n  is rebuilt-from-registry each render (a cache, not a source); drift-safe; deduped; rollback = stop\n  calling it.\n- **R5 â€” Context pollution degrades a skill (Contrarian F1).** *Status:* downgraded by John's\n  lived-workflow evidence; *mitigation:* the context-relief handoff (Â§4.4) gives clean context\n  whenever it's actually wanted, so context is never force-shared.\n- **R6 â€” Re-seeding a live PTY is unproven (SK-4/A2).** *Mitigation:* the default advance injects\n  NOTHING into the PTY (relabel+save only); the only PTY-writing path is the v11.1 handoff into a\n  FRESH session (already proven) + the opt-in \"load skill for me\" convenience, both flush-after-greet\n  with the v11.1 base-count guard captured from a re-seed cursor.\n- **R7 â€” Foreman builds in a dirty shared worktree (F3).** *Mitigation:* per-stage baseline commits\n  leave the tree in a clean committed state at build start; if a build needs a pristine checkout the\n  context-relief handoff gives it one. Validated in the healthcheck build walk.\n- **R8 â€” Restart mid-effort loses work (F6).** *Mitigation:* Â§4.4 restart recovery â€” persist active\n  stage, mark interrupted (not DONE), reopenable to continue.\n- **R9 â€” Concurrency: manual+auto advance race / advance-during-input (A7).** *Mitigation:* WRITE_LOCK\n  + idempotency guard in `advance_stage`; both manual and auto go through it.\n- **R10 â€” \"UI looks done but isn't\" + the f-string/RAW brace hazard (A9, the v4 lesson).**\n  *Mitigation:* render-smoke (balanced-brace import) before Playwright; every UI wave gated by DOM\n  pos+neg + Playwright/Chromium + screenshot-vs-mockup + John's sign-off. String-grep-only = HALT.\n- **R11 â€” Grass two-session ideas break under the one-session model (A10).** *Mitigation:* Â§4.7\n  back-compat render + test.\n- **R12 â€” Scope (F5).** *Mitigation:* inclusion test (every wave â†’ an SC); UI ships early decoupled\n  from the core; reuse-over-rewrite is a hard rule.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Done-when (Master-Plan level)\n\nOn a real project: start an effort, work in research, **Advance â†’** (or auto on a committed plan\nset) keeps the SAME session and migrates the tile to Plan/Build while persisting+summarizing the\nresearch stage; each stage's docs attribute only to that stage; a build resolves (or you pin) a\ndeliverable from build-stage docs only; when context fills, a one-click handoff continues the same\neffort in a fresh session; a service restart mid-effort recovers without loss; existing chains render\nas efforts with no double tiles and no destructive rewrite; the Layout-D dashboard + bottom dock +\ngrass workbench match the approved mockups; and `check_rnd_v12_surface` is GREEN fully stubbed â€” all\ninvariants intact, merged only after your per-UI-wave sign-off.\n\n---\n\n## Appendix â€” Shark-Tank Round 1 (2026-06-21)\n\n3 fresh-context Sharks (Skeptic / Contrarian / Analyst), each prompted to refute. **All 3 verdicts:\nBLOCK.** â‰¥2-agree BLOCKERs: doc-attribution in a shared worktree (SK-2+F2); summary cache key across\nstages (SK-3+A1); legacy auto-advance / orphaned advance endpoints spawn sessions (SK-1+A3). 3-way\nMAJOR: migration split-brain (F4+SK-6+A4). Premise challenge (F1, context pollution) **resolved by\nJohn's lived-workflow evidence** â†’ the continuity-first model with a context-relief handoff, which\nconverts every BLOCKER into a named, testable engineering item folded into Â§4/Â§6 above. Convergence\nauthority: John (locked the revised model + sequencing 2026-06-21).\n","numLines":387,"startLine":1,"totalLines":387}}}
