{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CSdwHhgjbJWboYtVHYhsz6","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Anchor R&D Surface v12 â€” \"Efforts\" (continuity-first single-session trio) â€” Implementation Plan (Foreman-ready)\n2\t\n3\t> Crucible Stage 2 output, 2026-06-21 â€” **revised after Shark-Tank Round 2** (3 fresh-context sharks:\n4\t> Sequencing BLOCK / Testability BLOCK / Completeness SHIP-WITH-FIXES; all findings folded in: complete\n5\t> retirement map gated on `effort_managed`, exact git mechanics, split over-bundled waves, UI shipped\n6\t> early as a static skeleton, falsifiable GWTs). Frozen design: `MASTER-PLAN.md`. Build cwd = repo root\n7\t> `C:\\dev\\Anchor`, branch `foreman/rnd-surface-v12` (off master `f2e0e40`, v11.1 merged + deployed).\n8\t\n9\ttest-command: python -m pytest -q\n10\t\n11\t## Conventions (read before any wave)\n12\t\n13\t- **Continuity-first model (locked).** An effort is ONE session by default; \"Advance\" = relabel +\n14\t  persist + summarize the completed stage (NO new session, NO PTY injection by default); a\n15\t  warn+one-click fresh-session handoff is the context-relief valve only; legacy chains render AS\n16\t  efforts via a non-destructive view layer.\n17\t- **The `effort_managed` discriminator (critical â€” Shark C3).** A v12 effort carries\n18\t  `effort_managed=True`, set ONLY by the v12 entrypoints (the \"+ New effort\" start, `handoff_to_fresh`,\n19\t  and `advance_stage`/`finish_stage`). Legacy records (incl. the synthetic projects in the v6/v8/v10/v11\n20\t  healthcheck walks) normalize to `effort_managed=False`. **Every retirement gate keys on\n21\t  `effort_managed`, never on `kind`/`current_stage`** (which legacy records also carry), so the legacy\n22\t  walks keep passing unchanged.\n23\t- **No live claude/gemini/real PTY:** stub via `tests/fake_claude.py` / `tests/stub_streamjson.py`;\n24\t  PTY via `ANCHOR_PTY_BACKEND=stub`; git via the `worktrees._git` seam; temp git/data dirs throughout.\n25\t  Never bind `:8777`, never touch real data/network; `ANCHOR_PROACTIVE_SUMMARY` off in tests.\n26\t- **THE v11 LESSON (non-negotiable).** Every advance/handoff/stage test is **worktree-only** (write\n27\t  produced docs into the session worktree, never `eh.record_effort` pre-persist) and, for\n28\t  conversation-only stages, **seed the stub PTY read buffer** via `pty_manager.write` (no file written).\n29\t  A pre-persisted test masks coverage. Each advance test asserts session-id **SET equality** (snapshot\n30\t  the id-set pre/post, assert equal â€” not just `len`) to survive reconcile churn.\n31\t- **pywinpty** lazy-only (`pty_manager.py`); **Playwright DEV-ONLY** (`pytest.importorskip`), never in\n32\t  product; `distro.py` scan green (new modules stdlib-only + in `dist_manifest.txt`).\n33\t- **Render discipline:** `render_project_window_html` is an f-string (double-brace `{{ }}`);\n34\t  `_PROJECT_WINDOW_JS` is a RAW single-brace string. A **render-smoke test** (import + non-empty\n35\t  balanced-brace HTML) precedes every Playwright wave.\n36\t- **UI verification (the v4 lesson)** on Waves 2, 10, 11: rendered-DOM (positive + negative) + a real\n37\t  Playwright/Chromium interaction test with **machine-checkable pass conditions** (not \"element exists\")\n38\t  + an orchestrator screenshot vs the named mockup **+ named deltas** (the warn banner + \"+ New effort\"\n39\t  are intentional additions beyond the mockup) + John's sign-off. A string-grep-only gate is an automatic\n40\t  HALT.\n41\t- **Baseline:** GREEN 1266, 1 skipped at branch cut. Each wave holds or grows. Best-effort keystones\n42\t  (persist/snapshot/summary/boneyard/view) NEVER break the operation they hook.\n43\t- **No merge to master / no `nssm restart` until John signs off.**\n44\t\n45\t---\n46\t\n47\t## Wave 1 â€” Effort record: stage fields + `effort_managed` + `effort_id` passthrough + back-compat normalize (backend)\n48\t\n49\t**Goal.** The session record can carry an effort's stage + the v12 discriminator without breaking any\n50\texisting record, and `start_session` can inherit an `effort_id`.\n51\t\n52\t**Changes.**\n53\t- `session_registry._normalize`: add `kind` (`\"trio\"|\"general\"|\"grass-dev\"`, derived from `lane` when\n54\t  absent), `current_stage` (`\"\"|research|plan|build`, from `lane` when absent), `stage_history` (list of\n55\t  `{stage, store_lane, started_at, ended_at|null, baseline_ref, seeded, summary_ref|null, doc_count,\n56\t  state}` where `state âˆˆ {active,done,interrupted}`; default `[]`), `seeded_stages` (list, default `[]`),\n57\t  `effort_id` (default = own `session_id`), `effort_managed` (bool, default **False**). All back-compat;\n58\t  an old record normalizes with no crash and `effort_managed==False`.\n59\t- `session_registry`: helpers `effort_root(sid)`, `set_current_stage(sid, stage, store_lane,\n60\t  baseline_ref)` (close prior entry â†’ append new), `stage_entry(record, stage)`.\n61\t- `terminal_session.start_session(..., effort_id=None, effort_managed=False)`: when `effort_id` is given\n62\t  the new record inherits it (else = own sid); `effort_managed` stored as passed. (No behavior change for\n63\t  existing callers â€” both default to today's behavior.)\n64\t- `anchor_gui`: a board-routing accessor `_effort_zone(record)` â†’ Research vs Plan/Build vs none (by\n65\t  `current_stage`/`kind`). **Render unchanged this wave** (the 5-col board still renders; the accessor is\n66\t  unit-tested only; its render consumer arrives in W10 â€” noted so a reviewer doesn't expect live routing).\n67\t- Audit `chain_members`/`_CHAIN_LANE_ORDER`/`_REGISTRY_LANE_TO_COLUMN` consumers; document that `lane`\n68\t  reads keep working when it later flips.\n69\t\n70\t**Done-when.** A pre-v12 record loads â†’ derived `kind`+`current_stage`, `stage_history==[]`,\n71\t`effort_id==sid`, `effort_managed==False`, round-trips unchanged in meaning; `start_session(effort_id=X,\n72\teffort_managed=True)` produces a record with