, buttons disabled/labeled \"(wired in W10)\"). Driven by the EXISTING\n102\t  `_gather_project_sessions` (already on master), mapped into the headline/shelf shape by a thin adapter.\n103\t  Keep masthead + lifecycle + GitHub controls. Preserve the f-string/RAW boundary.\n104\t\n105\t**Done-when.** The window renders Layout D matching the mockup (two headline cards, two collapsible\n106\tshelves, right column, + New effort, inert dock chrome); render-smoke + DOM pos/neg pass; Playwright\n107\tconfirms shelf collapse/expand; screenshot matches the mockup (+ named deltas: warn banner + New-effort);\n108\tJohn signs off the LOOK.\n109\t\n110\t**Given/When/Then.**\n111\t- *Given* a project with sessions, *When* rendered, *Then* DOM has one `.headline` (Latest Research) + one\n112\t  (Latest Plan/Build), each with a collapsible shelf of little tiles; a right column with Grass +\n113\t  Deliverables panels; a `+ New effort` control; an inert dock region (positive DOM). *Given* a project\n114\t  with zero sessions, *Then* honest empty states, no shelf, no crash (negative DOM).\n115\t- *Given* the page in Chromium, *When* a shelf \"Hide/Show all\" is clicked, *Then* it collapses/expands\n116\t  (the collapse state toggles a class â€” machine-checkable).\n117\t- **Render-smoke:** `render_project_window_html` imports + returns non-empty, brace-balanced HTML.\n118\t\n119\t**Tests.** `tests/test_layoutd_skeleton_v12.py` (DOM pos+neg + render-smoke) +\n120\t`tests/test_layoutd_skeleton_playwright_v12.py` (`pytest.importorskip`). Screenshot vs\n121\t`_mockups/dashboard_D_headline_shelf.html` + **John sign-off**.\n122\t\n123\t---\n124\t\n125\t## Wave 3 â€” Keystone A: per-stage baseline commit + stage-scoped persist + stage deliverable (backend)\n126\t\n127\t**Goal.** Each stage's produced docs (and the build deliverable) attribute to THAT stage only, even when\n128\tstages share one worktree. Fixes the doc-attribution BLOCKER (R1; SK-2/F2/B1/B2).\n129\t\n130\t**Changes.**\n131\t- `effort_history.record_stage_baseline(worktree_path)` â†’ commit (or capture a tree-ish) via\n132\t  `worktrees._git`; return `baseline_ref`. Best-effort.\n133\t- `effort_history.persist_session_stage_docs(folder, pid, sid, stage, store_lane, worktree_path,\n134\t  baseline_ref)` â€” produced set computed with **EXACT git commands** (no vague \"porcelain since baseline\"):\n135\t  `committed = git diff --name-only <baseline_ref>..HEAD`; `working = git diff --name-only <baseline_ref> --`\n136\t  (working-tree vs the baseline); `untracked = git status --porcelain -uall` filtered to additions; the\n137\t  produced set = `(committed âˆª working âˆª untracked)` **minus paths already attributed to a closed prior\n138\t  stage** (look up via `efforts_for_session_stage` for earlier stages). Persist+commit only those; tag\n139\t  each effort `(sid, stage)`. Add `efforts_for_session_stage(folder, pid, sid, stage)`. Keep legacy\n140\t  `persist_session_docs` for non-effort callers.\n141\t- `deliverables.resolve_build_deliverable`: when the subject is an effort, feed ONLY the build-stage doc\n142\t  set (`efforts_for_session_stage(..., 'build')`); honest unresolved when `current_stage != build` or no\n143\t  build-stage signal. `deliverables.backfill_build_deliverables`: same stage-filter (so rescan never pins\n144\t  a plan-stage MASTER-PLAN.md â€” Shark C6).\n145\t\n146\t**Done-when.** In ONE shared worktree where research committed `r.md` (baseline B0), then a plan baseline\n147\tB1, then `plan/MASTER-PLAN.md`, then a build baseline B2 and an UNCOMMITTED `app.py`: persisting the plan\n148\tstage yields `[planning/MASTER-PLAN.md]` only; persisting build yields `[app.py]` only; a build deliverable\n149\tresolves `app.py`, never `MASTER-PLAN.md`; and the legacy whole-tree diff is proven to return a superset.\n150\t\n151\t**Given/When/Then (ONE shared worktree, worktree-only).**\n152\t- *Given* one worktree W: commit `research/r.md`; B0=HEAD; B1=HEAD; commit `planning/MASTER-PLAN.md`,\n153\t  *When* `persist_session_stage_docs(...,'plan','planning',baseline=B1)`, *Then* persisted ==\n154\t  `[planning/MASTER-PLAN.md]` exactly; `efforts_for_session_stage(sid,'research')` == `[research/r.md]`;\n155\t  the two sets are disjoint. **Falsification (must be in the test body):** compute the legacy\n156\t  `_produced_doc_rels(W)` (whole-tree `diff HEAD` âˆª porcelain) in the SAME state and assert it returns a\n157\t  SUPERSET containing BOTH `r.md` and `MASTER-PLAN.md` â€” proving the stage-scoped result is a strict subset.\n158\t- *Given* the same W: B2=HEAD; write `build/app.py` **uncommitted**, *When*\n159\t  `persist_session_stage_docs(...,'build','build',baseline=B2)`, *Then* persisted == `[build/app.py]`;\n160\t  `MASTER-PLAN.md` excluded (predates B2, clean).\n161\t- *Given* an effort whose build stage produced `app.py` and plan stage `MASTER-PLAN.md` (one sid), *When*\n162\t  `resolve_build_deliverable`, *Then* `app.py` (honest unresolved if no build signal), never\n163\t  `MASTER-PLAN.md`; *When* `backfill_build_deliverables`, *Then* it pins `app.py` only. *Given*\n164\t  `current_stage=='plan'` â†’ resolved=False.\n165\t\n166\t**Tests.** `tests/test_stage_baseline_persist_v12.py`, `tests/test_stage_deliverable_v12.py`. No UI.\n167\t\n168\t---\n169\t\n170\t## Wave 4 â€” Keystone B: stage-keyed summaries + schema heal + closed-stage read via `store_lane` (backend)\n171\t\n172\t**Goal.** Each stage gets its own cached summary that resolves correctly even after `lane` flips. Fixes\n173\tthe summary-key BLOCKER (R2; SK-3/A1/B5).\n174\t\n175\t**Changes.**\n176\t- `summarizer.py`: thread an optional `stage` through `summarize_session`, `load_cached`, `summary_dir`,\n177\t  `_summary_json_path`/`_summary_md_path`, `session_blurb`, `session_doc_roles`; when `stage` given, cache\n178\t  dir = `<store_lane>/summaries/<sid>/<stage>/` (unchanged when absent). Bump `SUMMARY_SCHEMA_VERSION`\n179\t  2 â†’ **3** (concrete int so the heal test is falsifiable); an older/missing version is a MISS.\n180\t- The CLOSED-stage read path resolves via the stage's recorded `store_lane` (from `stage_history`), NOT\n181\t  the record's current `lane` (which has flipped).\n182\t\n183\t**Done-when.** Two stages of one session cache under distinct `<store_lane>/summaries/<sid>/<stage>/`\n184\tdirs; after the session's `lane` has flipped to a later stage, `load_cached(..., stage='research')` still\n185\tresolves the research summary via `store_lane`; an old single-key cache is a MISS.\n186\t\n187\t**Given/When/Then.**\n188\t- *Given* an effort whose research stage cached a summary, *When* the lane has since FLIPPED to `build`\n189\t  (`current_stage=='build'`), *When* `load_cached(..., stage='research')`, *Then* it resolves via\n190\t  `stage_history[research].store_lane`, NOT the current `lane`; AND `load_cached(stage='research') !=\n191\t  load_cached(stage='plan')` (no collision).\n192\t- *Given* a pre-bump (`SCHEMA_VERSION<3`) single-key cache at the OLD path, *Then* `load_cached` returns\n193\t  MISS (heals on next gen).\n194\t\n195\t**Tests.** `tests/test_stage_summary_key_v12.py`. No UI.\n196\t\n197\t---\n198\t\n199\t## Wave 5 â€” `finish_stage`: non-reaping durability refactor (backend, regression-only)\n200\t\n201\t**Goal.** Factor the persist+summarize keystone out of `kill` so a stage boundary persists+summarizes\n202\tWITHOUT reaping the worktree or marking the record terminal â€” with `kill` behavior provably unchanged.\n203\tFixes SK-7; isolates the delicate `kill` surgery (SEQ-4).\n204\t\n205\t**Changes.**\n206\t- `terminal_session.finish_stage(sid, stage, store_lane, project_id=None)` â€” `persist_session_stage_docs`\n207\t  (W3) + schedule the stage summary (W4), against the live worktree, **no reap, record stays RUNNING**.\n208\t- `terminal_session.kill` refactored to call `finish_stage` (current stage) then reap â€” its observable\n209\t  behavior (persist + boneyard + worktree removal + terminal status) **identical to today**.\n210\t\n211\t**Done-when.** `finish_stage` persists+summarizes a live effort's current stage with the worktree intact\n212\tand the record non-terminal; `kill` still persists, records the boneyard entry, removes the worktree, and\n213\tmarks the record terminal exactly as before (regression GREEN).\n214\t\n215\t**Given/When/Then.**\n216\t- *Given* a live effort, *When* `finish_stage`, *Then* docs persist (W3) + summary scheduled, worktree\n217\t  still on disk, record still RUNNING, no boneyard entry.\n218\t- *Given* a live session, *When* `kill`, *Then* identical to pre-refactor: docs persisted, boneyard\n219\t  `killed` entry recorded (when material), worktree removed, record terminal (regression assertions over\n220\t  the existing v8/v10 kill tests â€” they stay GREEN).\n221\t\n222\t**Tests.** `tests/test_finish_stage_noreap_v12.py` + the existing kill/boneyard suites stay GREEN. No UI.\n223\t\n224\t---\n225\t\n226\t## Wave 6 â€” `advance_stage`: in-session relabel+save + lock + idempotency (backend)\n227\t\n228\t**Goal.** Advancing a stage keeps the SAME session, injects nothing into the PTY, and is concurrency-safe.\n229\tFixes SC1 core; A7 concurrency; SEQ-9 (grass-dev acceptance).\n230\t\n231\t**Changes.**\n232\t- `terminal_session.advance_stage(sid, to_stage=None, mode=\"manual\"|\"auto\", project_id=None)` â€” take\n233\t  `paths.WRITE_LOCK`; validate a live effort of `kind in {'trio','grass-dev'}`; `to_stage` is the next\n234\t  stage; **idempotent** (no-op if `current_stage >= to_stage`); set `effort_managed=True`; `finish_stage`\n235\t  the current stage (W5); `record_stage_baseline` for the new stage; `set_current_stage`. **Inject NOTHING\n236\t  into the PTY** by default. (mode='manual' MAY accept `load_skill=True` to write one skill-load turn â€”\n237\t  explicit opt-in, default False; mode='auto' never writes.) Returns the updated record.\n238\t- `POST /api/rnd/advance_stage` (token-authed) â†’ `advance_stage(mode='manual')`.\n239\t\n240\t**Done-when.** Advancing a research effort to plan keeps the same `session_id`+`worktree_path`, persists+\n241\tsummarizes research, flips `current_stage`, sets `effort_managed=True`, with the session-id SET unchanged\n242\tand ZERO PTY bytes written; a concurrent manual+auto race yields exactly one advance.\n243\t\n244\t**Given/When/Then (worktree-only AND conversation-only).**\n245\t- *(worktree-only)* *Given* a live research effort with docs in its worktree only, *When*\n246\t  `advance_stage(sid,'plan','manual')`, *Then* same `session_id`+`worktree_path`; `set(list_sessions ids)`\n247\t  unchanged; `current_stage=='plan'`; research stage entry `state=='done'` with a `summary_ref`; plan\n248\t  entry `state=='active'`; `effort_managed==True`; **PTY buffer delta == 0**.\n249\t- *(conversation-only â€” the load-bearing case)* *Given* a live research effort whose ONLY output is\n250\t  transcript content seeded into its stub PTY read buffer via `pty_manager.write` (NO file, NO\n251\t  `record_effort`), *When* `advance_stage(sid,'plan','manual')`, *Then* research persists via the v11.1\n252\t  transcript-snapshot path (`research/<short-sid>-transcript.md` committed + tagged `(sid,'research')`),\n253\t  `current_stage=='plan'`, session-id set unchanged, **PTY buffer delta beyond the seeded transcript == 0**.\n254\t- *Given* `advance_stage` called twice (manual+auto race under the lock), *Then* exactly one persist + one\n255\t  summary + one flip; the second is a no-op.\n256\t- *Given* a `grass-dev` effort, *When* `advance_stage`, *Then* accepted (covers W11's reuse).\n257\t\n258\t**Tests.** `tests/test_advance_stage_v12.py`, `tests/test_advance_stage_conversation_v12.py`. No UI.\n259\t\n260\t---\n261\t\n262\t## Wave 7 â€” `detect_stage_progress` + the COMPLETE retirement map + term_sessions rewire (backend)\n263\t\n264\t**Goal.** Auto-advance fires only on a high-precision on-disk signal (never PTY scrape), and EVERY legacy\n265\tsession-minting path is gated off for `effort_managed` efforts so two advance models can never coexist.\n266\tFixes SC1; SK-1/A3/A5/B4/B7; **C1/C2/C3/C4** (complete map + correct discriminator).\n267\t\n268\t**Changes.**\n269\t- `terminal_session.detect_stage_progress(sid)` â€” on-disk only: researchâ†’plan iff a COMMITTED\n270\t  `MASTER-PLAN.md`+`IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN.md` pair with commit-time **newer than the stage start** exists;\n271\t  planâ†’build iff a committed EXECUTION-LOG / build product exists. **Reads ZERO PTY bytes.** Idempotent;\n272\t  conversation-only stages do NOT auto-advance (manual Advance â†’'s job â€” stated honestly).\n273\t- **Complete retirement map â€” gate on `effort_managed` at EVERY minting site:**\n274\t  `auto_advance_planning_to_build` AND its call sites: the `term_kill` handler branch\n275\t  (`anchor_gui.py:~11925`, **C1**), the `finish_to_build` handler (`:~12686`), and `reconcile_and_advance`\n276\t  (`:~11020`); the `/api/rnd/advance_session` + `/api/rnd/finish_to_build` handlers; and BOTH\n277\t  `_PROJECT_WINDOW_JS` buttons â€” the research **\"Advance to Planning â†’\"** bar AND the planning **\"Finish â†’\n278\t  Build â†’\"** bar (**C2**). Each early-returns (no mint) when the subject `effort_managed==True`. They stay\n279\t  fully live for legacy (`effort_managed==False`) records, so the v6/v8/v10/v11 healthcheck walks pass\n280\t  unchanged (**C3**).\n281\t- `anchor_gui`: rewire the `term_sessions` refresh to call `detect_stage_progress` for `effort_managed`\n282\t  efforts (instead of `reconcile_and_advance`).\n283\t\n284\t**Done-when.** A committed plan-set auto-advances an effort once (zero PTY reads); none of the six legacy\n285\tminting paths spawns a session for an `effort_managed` effort (session-id set unchanged at each); all\n286\tlegacy walks still mint as before for `effort_managed==False` records.\n287\t\n288\t**Given/When/Then.**\n289\t- *(pos)* *Given* an effort whose worktree gains a COMMITTED MASTER-PLAN.md+IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN.md pair\n290\t  newer than the stage start, *When* `detect_stage_progress`, *Then* it advances to plan ONCE (idempotent\n291\t  on re-poll), `set(list_sessions ids)` unchanged, ZERO PTY bytes read.\n292\t- *(neg, isolation)* *Given* a PTY buffer echoing \"Crucible loaded\" + a WORKING-TREE (uncommitted)\n293\t  MASTER-PLAN.md (no committed pair), *When* `detect_stage_progress`, *Then* NO advance (requires a\n294\t  committed pair newer than stage start) â€” proving it neither scrapes the PTY nor fires on uncommitted files.\n295\t- *(retirement, parametrized over ALL six paths)* *Given* an `effort_managed` effort at plan/DONE, *For\n296\t  each of* {`auto_advance_planning_to_build`, the `term_kill` branch, the `finish_to_build` handler,\n297\t  `reconcile_and_advance`, `POST /api/rnd/advance_session`, `POST /api/rnd/finish_to_build`}, *When*\n298\t  invoked, *Then* it early-returns and `set(list_sessions ids)` is identical (set-equality, not count).\n299\t- *(legacy intact)* *Given* a synthetic legacy planning record (`effort_managed==False`, as the v10/v11\n300\t  walks build), *When* the kill/auto-advance path runs, *Then* a build session IS minted (legacy behavior\n301\t  preserved).\n302\t\n303\t**Tests.** `tests/test_detect_stage_progress_v12.py`, `tests/test_retire_auto_advance_v12.py` (all six\n304\tpaths + legacy-intact). No UI.\n305\t\n306\t---\n307\t\n308\t## Wave 8 â€” Context-relief handoff (warn + one-click) + restart recovery (backend)\n309\t\n310\t**Goal.** When context fills (or on click), the effort continues in a fresh session that JOINS the same\n311\teffort; a restart mid-effort recovers without loss. Fixes SC2; F6/B6/B8/C7.\n312\t\n313\t**Changes.**\n314\t- `terminal_session.context_fullness(sid)` â†’ stdlib turn/byte-budget heuristic â†’ `{ratio, over_threshold}`.\n315\t- `terminal_session.handoff_to_fresh(effort_id_or_sid, project_id=None)` â€” `finish_stage` current stage â†’\n316\t  `prepare_stage_handoff` (v11.1) builds the real doc-referencing prompt â†’ `start_session(effort_id=<same>,\n317\t  effort_managed=True)` with the prompt as a **pending paste** (nothing auto-submitted). Old session's\n318\t  current stage entry â†’ `state=='done'`, worktree NOT reaped.\n319\t- `terminal_session.recover_interrupted_efforts()` â€” on boot/reconcile, an `effort_managed` record RUNNING\n320\t  but whose PTY is gone: persist the active stage (W5), mark that stage entry `state=='interrupted'` (a\n321\t  literal distinct from `done`/`failed`), keep reopenable to continue the SAME stage (a fresh session\n322\t  inheriting `effort_id`). NOT auto-advanced; NOT auto-spawned.\n323\t- Endpoints: `GET /api/rnd/context_status?session=` (read-only) + `POST /api/rnd/handoff_to_fresh`\n324\t  (token-authed). `anchor_gui` calls `recover_interrupted_efforts` on the reconcile path.\n325\t\n326\t**Done-when.** A one-click handoff yields a NEW session (distinct id) with the SAME `effort_id`, the prior\n327\tstage persisted, the next prompt held UNSENT; a simulated restart marks the active stage `interrupted`\n328\t(not DONE), no doc loss, reopenable, no auto-spawn.\n329\t\n330\t**Given/When/Then (worktree-only / conversation-only).**\n331\t- *Given* a running effort at `current_stage=='plan'` with plan docs in its worktree, *When*\n332\t  `handoff_to_fresh(effort_id)`, *Then* `new.session_id != old.session_id` AND `new.effort_id ==\n333\t  old.effort_id`; plan docs persisted+committed; `new.pending_paste==<prompt>` and `paste_flushed==False`;\n334\t  `pty_manager.read_since(new_sid,0)` contains the greet marker but NOT the prompt body (held unsent per\n335\t  the v11.1 base-count guard); `old.worktree_path` still exists (not reaped); old plan stage `state=='done'`.\n336\t- *Given* `context_fullness` over threshold, *When* `GET /api/rnd/context_status`, *Then*\n337\t  `over_threshold==true`.\n338\t- *(restart)* *Given* an `effort_managed` effort RUNNING at build with UNCOMMITTED build docs, simulate\n339\t  PTY-gone via `pty_manager.kill(sid)` WITHOUT `terminal_session.kill` (the reconcile-dead state), *When*\n340\t  `recover_interrupted_efforts`, *Then* build docs persist (worktree-only), the build stage entry\n341\t  `state=='interrupted'` (â‰  done, â‰  failed), the effort is reopenable to continue build (fresh session\n342\t  inherits `effort_id`), `set(list_sessions ids)` shows no auto-spawned build, and the v9 anchor-repo/\n343\t  live-member guard is not tripped.\n344\t\n345\t**Tests.** `tests/test_context_handoff_v12.py`, `tests/test_restart_recovery_v12.py`. No UI (the banner\n346\tis W10).\n347\t\n348\t---\n349\t\n350\t## Wave 9 â€” Effort view-layer: group chains into efforts (NEW `effort_view.py`) + dedup/drift (backend)\n351\t\n352\t**Goal.** Legacy chains and new single-session efforts render uniformly as efforts, from a derived,\n353\tdrift-safe, deduped view. Fixes SC7; F4/SK-6/A4/B9.\n354\t\n355\t**Changes.**\n356\t- NEW `effort_view.py` (stdlib only; added to `dist_manifest.txt`): `build_effort_view(folder, pid)` â€”\n357\t  group registry records by `chain_id`; emit ONE effort per chain `{effort_id (chain root), current_stage\n358\t  (most-advanced member), stage_history (synth from members â†’ each member's persisted docs + cached\n359\t  summary), status (newest member), live_worktree?}`. A new v12 single-session effort (already carrying\n360\t  `stage_history`) passes through as itself. **Rebuilt from the registry on every call** (a cache, not a\n361\t  source); a deleted member drops (no ghost stage); **deduped** so a chain member that is ALSO a live\n362\t  session carrying `stage_history` renders the effort exactly once (live status wins). Guarded like\n363\t  `project_move` (never the Anchor repo; reads, never reaps, live members). `effort_for_session(folder,\n364\t  pid, sid)`.\n365\t- `anchor_gui._gather_efforts(pid)` returns the view for the render layer (W10/W11); legacy\n366\t  `_gather_project_sessions` retained for fallback.\n367\t\n368\t**Done-when.** A project with a legacy 3-member chain AND one new single-session effort renders exactly\n369\ttwo efforts (no double tiles, no ghost stages); deleting a chain member drops only that stage; building\n370\ttwice is idempotent; the migration-overlap case (a chain member also live with `stage_history`) renders\n371\texactly once.\n372\t\n373\t**Given/When/Then.**\n374\t- *Given* a researchâ†’planâ†’build chain (3 records) + one new effort record with `stage_history`, *When*\n375\t  `build_effort_view`, *Then* exactly 2 efforts; the chain effort `current_stage=='build'` with 3 stages.\n376\t- *Given* the chain's plan member deleted, *When* rebuilt, *Then* research+build only (no ghost), no crash.\n377\t- *(dedup, SK-6)* *Given* a chain whose build member is ALSO present as a live registry session carrying\n378\t  `stage_history`, *When* `build_effort_view`, *Then* exactly ONE effort for that `chain_id` (len==1; live\n379\t  status wins).\n380\t- *Given* two builds, *Then* idempotent (equal); *Given* the Anchor repo, *Then* the guard holds.\n381\t\n382\t**Tests.** `tests/test_effort_view_v12.py`, `tests/test_effort_view_drift_v12.py`. No UI.\n383\t\n384\t---\n385\t\n386\t## Wave 10 â€” Wire Layout-D live: effort-view board + bottom dock (terminal + summary-on-top + Advance + warn) (UI-gated)\n387\t\n388\t**Goal.** The W2 skeleton goes live: headline/shelves driven by the effort view; the dock attaches a\n389\treal terminal with summary-on-top + a draggable height splitter + Advance + the context-full warn banner;\n390\tthe home dashboard rows reflect efforts. Fixes SC1/SC2/SC3 render; SEQ-1/2/7; A9/B10.\n391\t\n392\t**Changes.**\n393\t- `_PROJECT_WINDOW_JS` + render: bind the headline cards + collapsible shelves to `_gather_efforts` (W9);\n394\t  selecting an effort/tile opens the SINGLE bottom dock (replaces any floating stack): title bar (stage\n395\t  track + min/max/close + distinct **Kill â†’ Boneyard**), **summary on top (full width)** via reused\n396\t  `_renderSplitSummary`/`_loadPanelSummary`, a **draggable vertical splitter**, a **full-width terminal**\n397\t  whose height the user drags (reuse WSâ†’SSE transport + xterm mount/fit/ResizeObserver with a **debounced**\n398\t  splitter-drag fit). Wire **Advance â†’** (â†’ `/api/rnd/advance_stage`) and the **context-full warn banner**\n399\t  (polls `/api/rnd/context_status` â†’ one-click `/api/rnd/handoff_to_fresh`). The stage track relabels +\n400\t  the tile migrates zones on refresh.\n401\t- `anchor_gui`: home dashboard project rows reflect efforts (running-effort presence, latest objective,\n402\t  current stage) via the effort view; `GET /api/rnd/projects_html` covers the in-place refresh.\n403\t\n404\t**Done-when.** Clicking an effort opens the dock with summary-ABOVE-terminal, a live attached terminal\n405\tthat stays attached + fits while the splitter is dragged; Advance relabels in place with no new session;\n406\tthe warn banner appears on `over_threshold` and one click hands off; home rows show effort state; matches\n407\tthe mockup (+ named deltas); John signs off.\n408\t\n409\t**Given/When/Then.**\n410\t- *Given* a live effort, *When* its tile is clicked, *Then* the dock shows the summary panel ABOVE a\n411\t  full-width terminal (DOM order asserted), the terminal attaches, the stage track reflects `current_stage`.\n412\t- *(Playwright, machine-checkable)* *When* the splitter is dragged, *Then* (a) the xterm element is still\n413\t  in the DOM AND its transport `readyState===OPEN` (evaluate in-page), (b) a typed char round-trips into\n414\t  the terminal buffer after the drag, (c) `terminal.cols/rows` changed (fit ran). *When* **Advance â†’**\n415\t  clicked, *Then* `/api/rnd/advance_stage` is called and the stage track/zone updates with the session-id\n416\t  set unchanged. *Given* `context_status.over_threshold`, *Then* the warn banner renders; *When* clicked,\n417\t  *Then* `/api/rnd/handoff_to_fresh` is called once.\n418\t- *(neg)* *Given* no effort selected, *Then* no dock body bound (negative DOM).\n419\t\n420\t**Tests.** `tests/test_layoutd_live_v12.py` (DOM pos+neg + render-smoke) +\n421\t`tests/test_layoutd_live_playwright_v12.py` (clickâ†’dock-bound-to-effort_id, drag-splitter-WS-open+echo,\n422\tAdvance-no-new-session, warn-banner). Screenshot vs `_mockups/dashboard_D_headline_shelf.html` (dock open)\n423\t+ **John sign-off**.\n424\t\n425\t---\n426\t\n427\t## Wave 11 â€” Grass two-pane workbench (one session/idea) + General + Boneyard (UI-gated)\n428\t\n429\t**Goal.** Grass becomes the approved one-session-per-idea workbench (retiring the grass second-advance);\n430\tGeneral + Boneyard surface in Layout-D. Fixes SC5/SC6; A10/C4.\n431\t\n432\t**Changes.**\n433\t- `effort_history`: collapse the per-(idea,lane) `dev_sessions` map to a single stage-carrying dev session\n434\t  per idea (reuse W6 `advance_stage` within grass; the dev session is `kind=='grass-dev'`,\n435\t  `effort_managed=True`). **Retire the grass second-advance:** gate `advance_grass_research_to_plan` +\n436\t  `/api/rnd/grass_advance` + its JS button OFF for `effort_managed` ideas (route to in-session\n437\t  `advance_stage`), leaving them live for the legacy v10/v11.1 walks (same `effort_managed` discriminator â€”\n438\t  C4). **Back-compat:** an existing idea with two `dev_sessions` renders the most-advanced as the single\n439\t  workbench session with a stage history; no orphan. `grass_workbench_data` returns the single-session shape.\n440\t- `anchor_gui` + `_PROJECT_WINDOW_JS`: render `_mockups/grass_2_workbench.html` â€” left idea list (capture,\n441\t  search, filter chips, âœ•â†’Boneyard); right workbench (header w/ auto-saved indicator + **Migrate to\n442\t  project â†‘** + Archive snapshot; idea text; auto-gathered History + deliverable links; ONE session\n443\t  terminal + engine toggle; NO Research/Plan buttons). Migrate = `export_grass_to_project`; âœ• =\n444\t  `delete_grass_idea` â†’ Boneyard. General opens in the dock like any effort. Boneyard per-project tab\n445\t  (reuse `GET /api/rnd/boneyard` + search).\n446\t\n447\t**Done-when.** The grass workbench matches the mockup (two panes, one session, no R/P split, Migrateâ†‘,\n448\tâœ•â†’Boneyard); the grass second-advance is gated off for v12 ideas; an old two-session idea still renders +\n449\tworks; General opens in the dock; the Boneyard tab lists + searches discarded entries; John signs off.\n450\t\n451\t**Given/When/Then.**\n452\t- *Given* a grass idea, *When* the workbench renders, *Then* DOM has a left list + a right workbench with\n453\t  ONE session area and NO research/plan buttons (positive); *Given* a pre-v12 idea with\n454\t  `dev_sessions={research,plan}`, *Then* one session surfaces with a stage history, no orphan (back-compat).\n455\t- *Given* an `effort_managed` grass idea, *When* `advance_grass_research_to_plan` is invoked, *Then* it\n456\t  early-returns (no second grass session minted); the in-session `advance_stage` is used instead. *Given* a\n457\t  legacy idea (`effort_managed==False`), *Then* the old grass-advance still works (legacy walks pass).\n458\t- *(Playwright)* *When* **Migrate to project â†‘** clicked, *Then* `export_grass_to_project` called (idea\n459\t  stays, `grass_origin` stamped); *When* âœ•, *Then* `delete_grass_idea` â†’ the idea appears in the Boneyard\n460\t  tab (assert `GET /api/rnd/boneyard` contains it, not just that a toast fired).\n461\t- *Given* a project with discarded material, *When* the Boneyard tab + search, *Then*\n462\t  `GET /api/rnd/boneyard?q=` filters (positive); empty â†’ honest empty state (negative).\n463\t\n464\t**Tests.** `tests/test_grass_workbench_v12.py` (DOM pos+neg + back-compat + grass-advance retirement) +\n465\t`tests/test_grass_playwright_v12.py`. Screenshot vs `_mockups/grass_2_workbench.html` + **John sign-off**.\n466\t\n467\t---\n468\t\n469\t## Wave 12 â€” CLI mirror + `check_rnd_v12_surface` + distro + docs (PROJECT DONE)\n470\t\n471\t**Goal.** Read seams mirrored; the whole surface 